docs/DECISIONS.md:2824:Alex directs that the thesis-library evidence standard and prior hedge-fund analyst ledger review must both be applied, allows reasonable ambiguity, and asks to stop and leave a complete retrospective and current state. Both worktrees’ `AGENTS.md` §8 now point to the sources and require judging source, investment use and question admission separately. The eight-question research review is context, not a replacement for Alex’s decisions, adopted PRDs or frozen gold. Existing routing rules, including D209, remain unchanged. Gold examples inform judgment; optional details or differing labels do not become a rigid pass/fail. The [handoff](research/2026-10-29-claim-use/handoff-2026-10-29.md) preserves the failures, evidence, experiment limitations, active worktree and next task. No further experiment, product change, default switch, commit, push or deployment.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2826:## D229 · 2026-10-29 · The analyst standard for extraction is signed off and does not drift; measure Haiku against it
docs/DECISIONS.md:2828:- Alex, on [the standard](research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/standard.md) and its five open points (conditional valuation argument kept as supporting without a bare price target; post-earnings share reaction optional; four weight levels only, no numeric score; the pass line of §11; role-v23 after sign-off with one change per arm): "1-5 都可以，按照这套标准来开始做测量，这条标准不要漂移，放到agents.md 和memory 里面".
docs/DECISIONS.md:2829:- Decided: the standard is the one ruler for extraction gold, prompts, arms and acceptance; it changes only by a recorded decision in Alex's words. Both worktrees' `AGENTS.md` §8 point to it. The [gold check](research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/gold-check.md) applies: the frozen golds keep their files; the reference used from now on carries the four weight changes (two Alex's: revenue growth core, the 25-company letter supporting; two the assistant's, stated to Alex without objection: RTX 50 Super supporting, KeyBanc's Vera Rubin delay core), the three additions (AMD benchmark, FY2028 EPS, the conditional valuation) and the `fold_expected` cell for admission under ledger-blind extraction (D211).
docs/DECISIONS.md:2830:- Measurement, in this order: the per-article reference for the v38 week's 98 items and the 20-article holdout of 2026-07-08..14 (`holdout-pick.json`) written from the texts and frozen before any send; three gpt-6-luna draws of the production bytes and three Haiku 5.5 draws of the same text and schema (`haiku_week.py`, expected $0.78); every answer through the production sift; scored by the standard's §11 (structure by code, content by reading, core and supporting apart, no composite). role-v23 (the three conflicts in gold-check.md §5) is the arm after the measurement, not part of it.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2831:- Measured 2026-10-29 ([results](research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/results.md)): neither model meets every §11 pass line. Week / holdout: core every draw correct gpt-6-luna 41/45, Haiku 43/45 / both 3/3; supporting two of three 66/69 and 65/69 / both 15/16; the excluded Singapore case kept in every draw by both (7 items); must-propose raised every draw 6/23 and 7/23; ruled-out questions 15 and 30; unrelated statements (per-article medians summed) 464 and 286. Cost for 354 answers each: $0.457 and $0.886. The reference and labels are one reader's (Claude) and count as model-authored gold. No model or prompt change follows from the measurement by itself.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2841:- Decided: the Singapore case overview and its defendants' details are optional evidence (kept or omitted without penalty) wherever the reference or a gold marked them excluded under his question 5 (D215, gold v5 G05, standard §11's exclusion line). Whether a question may be opened from the case is still judged by the standard's §6 tests like any other matter; a court step against the defendants does not change an NVDA position, so such questions stay out. The role-v22 example "Singapore charged four firms over server exports" is no longer a conflict to fix.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2846:- The ruler was checked three ways ([results](research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/results.md), section 尺子核查): the raw answers, the model's own account of seven stored answers (the stored conversation continued, $0.010), and a blind second reader (Codex read-only, no model names, no labels) on 90 item cells and 80 unmatched records (88% agreement on the 84 comparable item cells). Five defects of the ruler were found and corrected, each written with its reason: four articles were asked for the obligation question though their text holds no guarantee, backstop or credit-support statement (now acceptable, not required); questions the production sift refused were read as not proposed (both counts now reported); article 352's relayed Kyber report and denial were missing (added as core); two 34x-input cells were over-credited; four partnership cells that drop the credit support the text names were over-credited. Reference v1 stays frozen; [reference v2](research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/reference-v2-changes.json) is frozen in `reference-v2.sha256`. Under v2 with the corrected labels: core every draw gpt-6-luna 41/47, Haiku 43/47; supporting 65/69 each; must-propose every draw 6 and 7 of 19 (7 and 10 counting questions the sift refused).
docs/DECISIONS.md:2853:- Decided: a record that writes an item's "this year" as the company's fiscal year containing the publication day (FY2027 for NVDA in July 2026), or as the calendar year, keeps the meaning; this matches the request's own fiscal-year note. The standard's example in §5 stays: turning "the rest of this year" into a full year changes the period and is a distortion. Gold v5's distortion "把今年余下时间改成 FY2027" no longer applies to the basis alone. Labels re-read under this rule: Haiku's third draw on 209 becomes correct; the other draws on that item still drop or deny the revenue measure.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2863:- Method ([results](research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/luna-results.md)): each arm replaces one sentence of the production extraction system text (role-v22, poc-v38 bytes; no prompt file edited), beside one fresh control per round with all jobs shuffled into one window, three draws, production sift, judgements registered before reading and read under hidden codes where reading was needed. Two subagents investigated only (quote-check census at $0; the model's own account of the missing Kyber question), writing to new folders. Cost $1.24.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2865:- No effect: two wordings of the standard's first test for opening a question (ruled-out 6 to 5 and 5; the excluded-kinds wording lost the obligation question on page 3); deleting the release-figures clause; tying kind (1) to the subject company.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2866:- For Alex: (1) the Kyber change rewrites the standard's main_driver ("承载公司价值的年度量") to include a product generation's launch or ship date; (2) the quote-check rule (typographic differences only, or also one elided run within a sentence, the stored quote restored to the source text; replay on 708 stored answers: 38 refusals to 24 or 35, no false accept read) changes what the system accepts; (3) ruled-out questions trace to the standard's own opening reasons (入股, 融资) without its 值得追 test, and two prompt wordings did not change them: a change to §6 or a code rule is his call. Nothing is adopted until the combined prompt is measured on the week and the holdout.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2871:- Decided, as proposed: (1) the standard's main driver also covers the launch or ship date of the product generation that carries the company's value; (2) the quote check accepts a quote that differs from the source only by punctuation, quotation marks or case, or by one run of words left out within one sentence, and stores the exact source text; (3) a binding obligation opens a question when the company guarantees, finances others, buys or backstops in its own name, or takes an equity stake whose size is stated and is not yet completed; its own borrowing does not open one. standard.md §6 is amended in these words.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2872:- Every prompt change is checked before the evaluation for wording tied to one company and for misfiring on other companies' material: the benchmark sentence tested in D235 rejected product and benchmark details "with or without a figure", which contradicts the standard's §2 ("没有业务规模的…跑分细节") and Alex's boundary ruling that a competitor's modelled comparison against the company's product is supporting (AMD 100 kW, 2.4x); it is rewritten to the standard's words and retested with two competitor-comparison articles outside the measured sets as guards.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2877:- Decided: the one-sentence arms of D232/D235/D236 were written against the bench pages' failures and checked on those pages; they are evidence of mechanisms, not the method. The extraction request is scrubbed as a whole: every rule and example must read the same for any covered company and sector; examples teach from varied domains and none comes from the test articles or names the covered company; the signed standard (D229, D231–D236) is the only source of rules. The scrubbed request is then measured once on the whole bench (the week's 98 articles and the 20-article holdout, three draws, reference v2, labelled in full like the baseline), and every number is reported against the role-v22 baseline, regressions first.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2883:- Done: six rounds on the 118 bench articles with gpt-6-luna, role-v24 to role-v29 (poc-v40 to poc-v45), each round read by hand and logged with its own mistakes (`docs/research/2026-10-29-analyst-standard/loop-2026-10-29/log.md`). Each rule comes from the signed standard (D229, §2 keep and reject lists, §6 opening reasons, §8 judgement 11), not from a new rule: another company's valuation, share price or deals that touch none of the company's markets, retail prices, content and compatibility details, and investors' trades are rejected even when a named party states them; a counterparty's or industry's statement that bears on demand, supply, input costs, competition, prices or products is kept; one deal, hire, programme or reported measure with its figures is one item; a reported announcement is a fact, rumour is what the item credits to unnamed sources; a guarantee or credit support for another party's debt, lease or revenue, financing to others, a purchase commitment or a backstop opens an obligation question whether or not the item gives its amount, while the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not; a launch or ship date opens only for the company's own product.
