docs/DECISIONS.md:2919:## D242 · 2026-10-29 · The standard becomes a web page, the extraction step's PRD; AGENTS.md and the README are cleaned and carry the prompt, measuring and iterating principles
docs/DECISIONS.md:2922:- Decided: `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html` (version 2.15) is the extraction step's PRD and the one source of the draft standard; its rules are those of `standard-v2.14.md`, which it supersedes, and it adds the golden set's results (§8) and how a prompt change is written, measured and iterated (§9, pointing to AGENTS.md). Its status is unchanged by this decision: a draft until Alex decides its twelve proposals; until then the signed standard (D229) is the only ruler and no prompt changes (D241). AGENTS.md §8 points to the page; §6 (writing prompts) and §7 (measuring and iterating, split into the ruler, reading results and iterating) carry the principles that were missed in earlier rounds, each with Alex's words or the incident behind it; outdated statements were removed (the design-phase "no product code" rule, a function that no longer exists, the old glossary section name). Two principles quote Alex's words from earlier the same day, recorded here as their source: on iterating, "你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression"; on self-graded measurement, "你的这个垃圾代码和尺子根本就是fucking cancer 我根本无法相信你的评价". The same AGENTS.md is in both worktrees. The README of each branch describes that branch. A read-only Codex review checked the rewrite against the old file and the decisions, and the page against v2.14 (`review-agents-rewrite.md`, `review-page-v2.15.md`); its confirmed findings were fixed, among them a D240 rule written stronger than Alex's words, a calibration step he never asked for, and 49 golden entries without speaker or meaning, now filled from the text.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2924:## D243 · 2026-10-29 · The extraction standard is signed: proposal 5 stricter, the other eleven at their leans; lean cautious, catch the increment
docs/DECISIONS.md:2926:- Alex, on the twelve proposals of `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`: "5. 这种典型的主张背景属于常识，基本上抽出来也没有太多的意义除非带数字和具体的叙事不然都是属于不采纳"; "然后你基本上也理解了这个核心，不是什么事情都是惊弓之鸟需要抽取，杂音还是很大的，我们整体应该倾向谨慎不要看什么都是线索的感觉，但是同时我们要敏感一些新的信息带来的增量不要错过"; "其他几条的意见我都ok，sign off, 你重新整合这个prd 和agentmd and readme 我们要开始重新跑了".
docs/DECISIONS.md:2929:- The known code defect of the standard (B17) is fixed: the year limit counts a fiscal-year form in the company's own fiscal years (`extraction.beyond_next_year`); in the stored role-v29 answers it had refused 2 of 40 candidates with a year (NVIDIA FY2028 in July 2026). Test `tests/test_fiscal_year_horizon.py` on two stored candidates; the mutant that drops the fiscal shift fails it.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2933:- Alex: "1. 好你来定 test validation split"; "2. 我觉得这是最容易出错的问题；你非常容易写死，我们在改的过程中如果drift你会一直用久的标准来衡量，这边需要有打分，但是“一定”要你自己下去看trace这是必须，记起来"; "3. v29 你先能跑出第一版的基线".
docs/DECISIONS.md:2934:- Decided: (1) the split is Claude's: the 118 bench articles, all seen, are the development set used for iterating and reading; a fresh test set from a later window no run has read is written from the text and frozen before its first send, and is scored once per configuration, never tuned on. (2) Every measurement has a score and Claude reads the traces: the raw answer beside the article, for every missed core or supporting entry and a sample of the extras and of the hits; a score is a lead, never the conclusion. The scorer hard-codes no rule of the standard: it reads the gold file it is given, prints the gold's and the page's sha256 and refuses a gold whose standard field names another page; a score is compared only with scores on the same gold; when the standard changes, the gold is re-derived and re-frozen before the next score. (3) The first task is the role-v29 baseline on the development set, three draws.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2950:- Decided: `scripts/replay.py` defaults to `poc/config/poc-v69.json`, which differs from `poc-v67` only in the ten extraction prompt versions (T*-v53). role-v53's role text is role-v51's unchanged; from version 53 the schema carries descriptions of `speaker`, `original_who` and `original_day` (`extraction.FIELD_NOTES`; standard 5.4 and 5.5, D203, D220, the signed gold's who column), and every earlier version's schema is byte-identical (`tests/test_field_notes.py`).
docs/DECISIONS.md:2951:- Measured (`loop-log.md` rows 26–33, `research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/fields-2026-10-30/`): writing the same definitions into the role text (role-v52) fixed the fields but kept about 7–15 more gold-rejected statements per draw; in the schema, against role-v51 sent together (run U, development + test, three draws): outlet-as-speaker and report-day signals 166 → 35 over 148 articles × 3 draws; verified field errors on a blind read of 24 fresh articles 18/96 → 11/94 records; gold-rejected statements kept −6.7 per draw; core per draw −1.3 and supporting at least two draws −4, both inside their paired intervals; must-open raised in every draw 17 → 22. Two follow-ups did not beat it and are not adopted: role-v54 (the role text's attribution clause removed) and role-v55 (the tier rule moved to the schema, refuted on its small sample). Left open: an author's restatement of another company's reported figures is still credited to the author (role-v56, which removes the T7 and T8 attribution phrases, is built and unsent).
docs/DECISIONS.md:2955:- Alex, on the census of duplicate and trivial questions: "我们的标准要收口"; then "你要不要深度的写好plan, 怎么测量，golden 是怎么，我们来解决这个问题；整体不能regress，你要秉持我们过往工程的原则，以及作为一个hedge fund analyst 到底怎么判断合并，去重，这个标准很重要，不能观点爆炸"; then, not following the plan's table, "我没理解每个难点，我需要一个一个和你过，你讲人话给我例子". Each boundary was put to him with an example and two options; his replies are quoted per row. Plan, census and review rounds: [question-identity plan](research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md) §0–§4, §11b, §12.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2959:  1. **One plan, several wordings** (H1, "A"): wordings of one plan whose final check is the same number are one question; two numbers that move on their own and are watched separately stay apart; a single deal under a plan already opened by amount merges into it. Not put to Alex: a not-yet-signed deal's yes/no signing question (D210; PRD 06 keeps number and event questions apart) stays as it is and does not merge into a plan's amount question (the Ohio lease guarantee and the cloud-customer total in v38 both stay). Narrows the standard §4 "another quantity in the same deal (a guarantee beside a financing)" sentence taken from D190; consistent with D210.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2964:  6. **Small matters opened as questions** (H6, "A， A"): a deal, product or project (the question was put about small deals and products) opens a question only when its scale can change the company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk; otherwise no question opens, and whether its statement is kept follows the evidence rule (standard §5). Done in this round together with the merge changes, each measured as its own arm, then together on the holdout. Narrows the standard §3 class C ("a sized, not yet completed stake or acquisition").
docs/DECISIONS.md:2966:- Next, in this order: the signed standard page (§3 class C, §4 "same question, succession or another question") carries these rules, then a read-only Codex drift review; then the plan's step 1 (structured census, the fixed-extraction replay harness, gold G1–G3, the September holdout week on Alex's go).
docs/DECISIONS.md:2970:- Alex, after a second-turn probe judged statements by standard 5.1 correctly that the one-pass answer had kept: "那为什么你不在prompt 里面要求做完自己复核一边就好，这样就是一个call完成"; then "你尝试一组先吧，这个完全就是再prompt 的最后面要求做完一遍基于"你刚才说的复核条件"再跑一次；写在同一个提示词里面"; then "可以，但是这个做法是有效的对吧，那你应该好好地写复核的侧重点然后跑；这个如果有效可以记录下来这个做法"; then the goal "你需要让这个加到prompt里面的方式improve performance. 一定要improve but don't hardcode or break our principles".
docs/DECISIONS.md:2971:- Decided (the method, written at AGENTS §6): from role-v59 the extraction request ends with a check that reads the evidence list back by standard 5.1 (`prompts/review-v<N>.txt`, `extraction.REVIEW_FROM`) and names no empty-answer condition; the role text of role-v59 to role-v63 is role-v53's. Every line of the check cites the standard (§5.1, §5.3, §6, D238, D243, D240); six read-only Codex rounds (`research/2026-10-30-noise/codex-review-*`); examples from other industries.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2975:## D250 · 2026-10-31 · Four evidence boundaries and the counting unit settled; the ruler is fixed before any further measurement (standard version 5)
docs/DECISIONS.md:2977:- Alex, on the ruler check of the not-kept statements role-v63 keeps (`research/2026-10-30-noise/ruler-check-2026-10-31.md`; a blind reader agreed with the gold on 93–95% of the controls and on 70% of the entries v63 kept) and the five places put to him with a lean each: "五处都按你的倾向定，计数单位也改; 你要修正尺子；你已经多次因为尺子标准问题陷入假的测量".
docs/DECISIONS.md:2981:  3. **A comparison the company, a partner or a third party publishes** ("10x lower cost than closed models", "40% more GPUs in the same power budget", a third party's test): the lean as put: "标准只说'对手拿来和本公司比'的要按 5.1 判；其余的都算产品细节，不收". A partner's or customer's adoption or integration in the same sentence is not dropped by this rule and is judged by 5.1 as before (the lean says nothing about it; an unconditional keep would be a new rule); ruling 4 (a competitor's 2.4x, supporting) unchanged.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2982:  4. **A named analyst's view of a new event** ("a Kyber delay widens the window for alternatives"): the lean as put: "只是解读一件已经记下的事、没有新事实或推算的，不收". One that adds a new fact or calculation is judged by 5.1; the conditional valuation (5.3) is unchanged.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2983:  5. **The counting unit**: the lean as put: "只有当那条记录本身不是该留的事，才算留了杂音". A not-kept gold entry counts as kept only when the record that carries it is not itself the same matter as a core, supporting or optional gold entry (optional is never penalised); not-kept words that ride inside the quote of a kept matter are one record of that matter ("一件事用几句话说仍是一条", standard §2).
docs/DECISIONS.md:2984:- The ruler (Alex: "你要修正尺子"): the standard page goes to version 5 with these rules, then a read-only drift review; the gold's evidence part is re-derived for version 5 (version 4 changed no evidence entry, `gold-v4-evidence-check.md`) by two independent readers with every disagreement decided against the article, written as a new frozen file with every change listed (before, after, reason), the version-3 file untouched (D243 item 11); the opening part of the gold is not re-derived here and the scorer reports no question score until it is. The scorer refuses a gold whose evidence part was made for another version of the page: `final_scores.py` had bypassed `score_gold.py`'s version check and scored rounds since D248 on the version-3 gold, which is the false measurement Alex names.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2985:- Not decided here: the financing-analysis entries (an IRR scenario, a debt-service floor) the blind reader would keep; they are judged by 5.1 in the re-derivation like any entry not on the 5.3 list.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2990:- Decided: when (and only when) the architecture is adopted after the measurement in design.md, the open-question list an extraction request shows is a snapshot frozen once per day; every article of that day sees the same list; the archive key is (item, snapshot hash); a day in flight never re-sends an item because the ledger moved. This narrows D211 ("the request depends on the item alone") to "depends on the item and the day's snapshot". Not decided: whether other companies' questions are shown, whether the one-home rule (D207) moves into the extraction prompt, what happens to a failed candidate's evidence; the measurement's predictions P1–P6 are frozen in design.md (sha256 in `predictions.sha256`).

